## Report
Validated the finding at commit 2b4ea5d0683b075d83fa943de7540bba318544ce. Code review confirms the race shape: peer workers call the serialized helper and exit on checkpoint failure at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:1703-1713; the helper takes durable_checkpoint_lock at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:1760-1770; the peer listener is started before startup checkpointing at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:1840-1850; startup still calls authority.store_durable_restart_artifact directly without that lock at crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:1860-1862 and 1879-1881. The durable writer uses File::create/write/sync then fs::rename on a temp path at crates/storage/src/control_plane_raft.rs:4019-4035, and that temp path is deterministic per destination basename and process id at crates/storage/src/control_plane_raft.rs:4961-4967. Dynamic validation succeeded twice. First, an integration PoC using the real ControlPlaneRaftRestartArtifact writer concurrently failed reliably: `cargo test -p storage --features test-hooks --test durable_race_poc -- --nocapture` exited 101 with multiple panics on `Io { context: "commit control-plane OpenRaft durable restart artifact", source: Os { code: 2, kind: NotFound, message: "No such file or directory" } }`. Second, an end-to-end process probe built and launched the real argmin-s3 binary as user nobody, waited for the experimental Raft peer Unix socket, and flooded it during startup. It reproduced the production failure mode on attempt 0: `experimental OpenRaft control-plane durability checkpoint failed after peer RPC; exiting to avoid serving volatile committed state: commit control-plane OpenRaft durable restart artifact: No such file or directory (os error 2)`. Valgrind was attempted but is not installed in the container. LLDB was available and a breakpoint/backtrace at Rust panic was captured in the artifacts.

